{
  "_comment": [
    "TEMPLATE — copy to google-services.json and fill in from YOUR OWN Firebase project.",
    "The real file is gitignored (ADR-0025): AllisWell ships every line of Firebase",
    "wiring, and none of the identifiers that point at the maintainer's project.",
    "",
    "Get yours: Firebase console > Project settings > Your apps > Android > google-services.json,",
    "or:  firebase apps:sdkconfig ANDROID <appId> --project <yourProject> \\",
    "       --out apps/app/android/app/google-services.json",
    "",
    "WITHOUT this file the app still builds and runs — the Gradle plugin is applied",
    "conditionally and Firebase reports itself unconfigured. See docs/FIREBASE.md.",
    "",
    "None of these values is a secret in the password sense: they ship inside every",
    "installed app and Google treats them as public identifiers. They are kept out of",
    "the repository because they POINT AT a billed project, not because they unlock it.",
    "What actually protects the project is Firebase Security Rules, App Check and the",
    "SHA-256 fingerprints registered for OAuth — configure those, do not rely on hiding",
    "this file."
  ],
  "project_info": {
    "project_number": "000000000000",
    "project_id": "your-firebase-project-id",
    "storage_bucket": "your-firebase-project-id.firebasestorage.app"
  },
  "client": [
    {
      "client_info": {
        "mobilesdk_app_id": "1:000000000000:android:0000000000000000000000",
        "android_client_info": {
          "package_name": "com.alliswell.alliswell"
        }
      },
      "oauth_client": [],
      "api_key": [
        {
          "current_key": "YOUR_ANDROID_API_KEY"
        }
      ],
      "services": {
        "appinvite_service": {
          "other_platform_oauth_client": []
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "configuration_version": "1"
}
